## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to justify product bets with a pragmatic, numbers-driven approach and to handle uncertainty in inputs.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation
- Benefit estimation
- Break-even analysis
- Reasonable assumptions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple CBA calculator
function cba(params) {
  const {maU, lift, arpu, months, cost} = params;
  const annualizedBenefit = maU * lift * arpu * months;
  return {annualizedBenefit, cost, breakevenMonths: cost / (annualizedBenefit || 1)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust if MAU grows or adoption changes?
- What if ARPU uplift is not uniform across user segments?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ability to design a financially justified, privacy-conscious payment feature that hinges on hardware-assisted security. It requires mapping costs to real-world constraints (region rollout, compliance, energy), and deriving Go/No-Go thresholds with a clear break-even horizon.

## Key Concepts

- On-device security (TEE, secure element)
- Card-not-present risk scoring and decision latency
- Multi-region rollout and regulatory compliance
- Cost drivers: licensing, key management, telemetry, energy
- Break-even calculation and ROI signaling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo on-device risk decision (sketch)
function shouldAuthorizeLocally(riskScore, latencyMs) {
  const threshold = 0.6;
  const fastPath = latencyMs < 200;
  return riskScore < threshold && fastPath;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate regional data privacy compliance and audits?
- What telemetry would you collect to monitor drift without leaking PII?

## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
CBA for an offline-first backup feature requires tangible cost knobs and measurable outcomes beyond accuracy or latency; beginner-friendly but demonstrates ability to quantify trade-offs and plan rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Energy budgeting per photo and dedup impact
- Data minimization and privacy/compliance
- Rollout, offline fallback, drift/maintenance, break-even

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo energy check before upload
function shouldUpload(photoSizeMB, currentEnergyJ, thresholdJ){
  const dedupFactor = 1.5;
  const energyPerMB = 0.25;
  const energy = photoSizeMB * energyPerMB * dedupFactor;
  return (currentEnergyJ - energy) > thresholdJ;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure de-dup effectiveness in production?
- What metrics trigger rollback during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model privacy-preserving analytics, not ML, with real-world trade-offs across storage, compute, energy, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy budgets & CRDTs for local aggregation
- Edge-resource constraints and telemetry design
- Compliance costs and regulatory penalties

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CRDT-like Grow-Only Counter
class GCounter { constructor() { this.counters = new Map(); }
inc(k, v=1){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0)+v,0)); }
merge(other){ for(const [k,v] of other.counters){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0), v)); } }
value(){ let s=0; for(const v of this.counters.values()) s+=v; return s; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CRDT reconciliation when offline and merging after sync?
- What metrics would you track to detect drift in your aggregates and how would you price the analytics feature?
